**Finding submitted: deviation (medium), § 13 (p0047).**

The agreement does contain a non-solicit binding us (contrary to the planner's "likely absent" hint) — it is buried at the end of the numbered clauses that the outline folds into § 7. On review it is already largely within our fallback:

- **Mutual** — binds both Clear Capital and RadialSpark;
- **Duration**: term plus one (1) year — well inside the 24-month walk-away limit;
- **Scope**: only personnel "who have had direct involvement with the Services," not all personnel;
- **Solicitation only** — no no-hire prohibition, so no walk-away trigger.

The single gap is the absence of a general-solicitation carve-out. Rather than strike the clause to reach the preferred position (no non-solicit on Customer), I made the minimal fallback edit adding carve-outs for general advertisements not targeted at the other party's personnel and for unsolicited approaches — consistent with the Harbor Consulting precedent. Redline validated ok:true.
